{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467663-how-to-do-kindred-of-africa-in-a-taste-for-fashion","id":1467663,"title":"How to do kindred of Africa in a taste for fashion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-13T01:16:29-08:00","id":1467663,"title":"How to do kindred of Africa in a taste for fashion","content":"How to do kindred of Africa in a tasteful fashion?<br /> <br /> First off allow me to say that I am running a LARP for a significant number of people (following all legal covid regulations of course), and as of late, the courts of Africa have come up. <br /> <br /> I have recently been given the task of trying to handle this particular conundrum. It strikes me as necessary that some rethinking of the book kindred of the Ebony kingdom must be done. While perhaps not intentionally insensitive in any fashion, the book has received criticism that it was not especially well thought out by the standards of our present day. <br /> <br /> I have hardly read it and have no opinion of it myself. It could be that the book is quite good. <br /> <br /> One of my players immigrated from Africa and he said that he thought the book was fine but not great and the majority of his criticisms were actually that it was outdated and also lacking in nuance when it came to depicting cultures, but not insensitive. I suspect he also doesn\u2019t want to say anything negative or positive for fear that he will steer the entire group into backing whatever he says without them doing any critical thinking on their own. Rather, I know he fears that because I asked him straight out and he said yes. <br /> <br /> I am trying to utilize African vampires in the current setting and I am somewhat at a loss. I want to represent the courts of Africa but could use a hand. Of course I turned to dark ages 20 and more importantly, the African people I know, but only one can speak to the game without being rather bewildered!<br /> <br /> DA20 has a number of bloodlines and clans which we are done in a unique and, I feel, well thought out way . But I could use a little bit more for the modern nights and I am in a bit of a bind. Some players say just don\u2019t mention it at all, other players say, that leaves us wondering if there are any vampires in Africa, and if so who? The courts of Africa need to come up in the LARP, and with a significant player base, I need to find something that will resonate Or at least not disappoint the player base","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T03:30:58-08:00","id":1467667,"title":"","content":"Well africa's a continent so which countries are we specifically discussing here?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T04:20:55-08:00","id":1467668,"title":"","content":"Remember that &quot;Africa&quot; is a modern place with some places heavily urbanized and some not at all. The absolute majority are just people living their lives like people do, with various levels of quality of life. Urbanites of Lagos are not that different from the urbanites of New York, and farmers in Senegal would likely find common ground with Texans.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/49/43/df/4943dfa69d79948e538f99a66dbd6249.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://theecologist.org/sites/default/files/styles/inline_l/public/2019-09/screenshot_2019-09-11_at_16.13.04.png?itok=nWogtY3s\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Now, when it comes to vampires, I'm leery of relying on averages. Vampire communities are too small for statistical analysis to apply to them. Certain social groups, mindsets, levels of education, etc. may easily be over-represented among vampires. Vampires are not representative of the communities that they prey on, and it gets worse as vampires get older and communities move on. Retainers are a handy way to show it - even if all your vampires are highly religious professional occultists, their retinue can hammer home that this is a vampire thing, not a &quot;person from Africa&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> But yeah. I'd say the most important thing is to avoid doing the Kuei-Jin schtick. These are not incomprehensible alien horrors beyond the American ken. These are your fellow undead dudes from abroad who are probably kinda assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T12:34:59-08:00","id":1467706,"title":"","content":"Considering what your friend said and what I read myself in the book, it seems the problem is that KotEK didn't actually go in detail about how those vampires organize there as it avoided going in detail describing the place at all. Which is a sensible choice given they didn't actually had the page count to make it work, but leaves an obvious vacuum.<br /> <br /> So I'd say you won't find your answer in WoD books at all because the issue is lack of RL information, and that's what you need to get. You don't need to decide how the courts of Africa are, you have to decide how vampires from different parts of Africa are.<br /> <br /> It helps that you won't actually make a game settled in Africa, so you only have to know how things are from the PoV of immigrants, but you'll need some points to drive it home still.<br /> <br /> Ask for help from your friend and get a number of regions in the continent you're actually going to work with. It's probably a good idea to include the countries of any immigrant or descendant player that may show up, maybe their neighbors, but try to keep it small so your work is feasible.<br /> <br /> Then forget the game for a while and take a look at how life in those areas is for some slices of the population. You don't need to dive too deep, counting on the accounts of natives help a lot. The most important is probably to take note of things natives have conflicting views about, that way you can apply nuance more easily.<br /> <br /> Doing this is a lot of work, but less than it seems at first. As you read or hear about your subject pieces will go in place on their own most of the time. Just take notes and in the end you'll have a clear picture, not of how the courts of Africa are, but of how to use them as background to the actual game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T20:26:42-08:00","id":1469803,"title":"","content":"There's a book called The Ebony Kingdom that might help as well. It was White Wolf's setting for Africa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T07:41:10-08:00","id":1469834,"title":"","content":"Truly, the most likely scenario is... <br /> The Camarilla, that global conspiracy that people keep forgetting is meant to be global. <br /> But the vampires are -insert ethnic group here- <br /> <br /> You can have fun with the occasional pre-sect grognard who lives like it's still the medieval period or his rabble of &quot;anarchs&quot; who have been taught to see the Camarilla as a foreign power, especially in less developed regions, but really the ideas of the Camarilla would've caught on. Thinking africa needs it's own sect is just radical sillyness that is pretty patronizing when you think about it enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}